Every fix run also needs a reviewer: a different model that only reads the change. Claude Code and Codex can write but cannot review.

Step 2 · The sandbox (rootless Podman)
  would ask: Create the Podman machine your Sessions run in?
      podman machine init --cpus 2 --memory 7168 --disk-size 60
      podman machine start
    This downloads about 0.9 GB and uses up to 7 GiB of memory while it runs. This size has not been tested yet (6 CPUs / 8 GiB is). [Y/n]
    would run: podman machine init --cpus 2 --memory 7168 --disk-size 60
    would run: podman machine start
  would ask: Check the sandbox with one throwaway container? This pulls docker.io/library/alpine:3.20 (about 4 MB), the image Sessions start from, and runs it rootless with your user mapped in and no network. [Y/n]
    would run: podman pull docker.io/library/alpine:3.20
    would run: podman run --rm --pull=never --userns=keep-id:uid=1000,gid=1000 --user 1000:1000 --network=none --cap-drop=all --security-opt=no-new-privileges docker.io/library/alpine:3.20 id -u

