Step 6 · Start Axocoatl
  How should Axocoatl run?: In this terminal now (axocoatl dev)
  would ask: Run a first fix now on a small sample repository to prove the setup end to end? It runs locally. [Y/n]

Step 7 · A first run
    would copy the sample repository to a temporary directory, SAMPLE, and run: axocoatl run fix --task 'Fix the bug: paging skips the last item' --repo SAMPLE/repo --receipt SAMPLE/receipt.json --record SAMPLE/record.jsonl --config '/var/folders/20/jp1_0n3n7kndh6rnbqb5344m0000gn/T//axo-gate-b.1R9RwS/plan-no-machine/Library/Application Support/Axocoatl/config.yaml' --model writer=ollama:qwen3-coder:30b --model reviewer=ollama:gpt-oss:20b
    would then run: axocoatl receipt verify SAMPLE/receipt.json --key "$(axocoatl receipt key)" --repo SAMPLE/repo

Next, in your own repository (start Axocoatl first with `axocoatl dev` if it is not running):
  cd ~/src/my-app
  axocoatl run fix --task "Describe the bug"
(writer ollama:qwen3-coder:30b, reviewer ollama:gpt-oss:20b come from your setup; --model ROLE=PROVIDER:MODEL overrides them)
  would start: axocoatl dev --config /var/folders/20/jp1_0n3n7kndh6rnbqb5344m0000gn/T//axo-gate-b.1R9RwS/plan-no-machine/Library/Application Support/Axocoatl/config.yaml

